cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use courtpy in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "courtpy: Accessible tools for collecting, parsing, and analyzing court opinions"
abstract: >-
  A Python package that collects court opinions (from CourtListener and
  Lexis-Nexis), turns them into data by parsing and coding them, adds the
  judges and the politics of the day, and analyzes the results, designed for
  reproducible empirical legal research.
authors:
  - given-names: Corey Rayburn
    family-names: Yung
    email: coreyrayburnyung@gmail.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6524-9956"
version: 0.2.3
date-released: 2026-10-17
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/WithPrecedent/courtpy"
url: "https://WithPrecedent.github.io/courtpy"
keywords:
  - court opinions
  - courtlistener
  - empirical legal studies
  - judges
  - law
  - open science
  - reproducibility
  - text parsing
